  "interpretation": [
    "At equal optical exposure the encoded RAW signal is approximately 0.63-0.64 times SDR100, not 1 times.",
    "This rejects only a pure metadata change that leaves the RAW values identical to ISO100. In-camera digital rescaling is still consistent with the observation.",
    "The additional full-green-plane test finds thousands of ISO64 pixels above raw 12000, beyond the simplified post-16383-clipping, black-aligned 0.64-pull ceiling of 10848. That specific simple pull model is inconsistent with these data; different internal precision or scaling stages remain possible.",
    "At equal optical exposure, matched-mean noise is broadly similar; no robust ISO64 advantage is established by this small sample.",
    "ISO64 at f3.2 receives about 1.56 times the light of ISO100/NLog800 at f4; its lower matched-mean noise must not be attributed solely to an intrinsic gain advantage."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "The 0.625 DN offset remaining in the continuous transfer is explicitly assessed; values are decoder coordinates, not electron counts.",
    "Gain may be analog, digital, or mixed. These measurements do not distinguish native from digitally pulled ISO by themselves.",
    "Separate recordings, fixed ROIs, 16-frame temporal samples, shared open-source decoder. The added full-plane ceiling test checks a simplified model, not an independently calibrated physical white level.",
    "Handwriting noise output is retained but is not used for sensor-noise conclusions because of structured edges.",
    "sigma_ratio_dividing_iso64_by_nominal_0p64 is a scale-normalization diagnostic; in the different-aperture comparison it does not also normalize the incident light."
  ],
  "measurement_method": {
    "frame_count_per_temporal_group": 16,
    "noise_roi": "door_shadow",
    "pixels_per_channel": 147456,
    "temporal_statistic": "Remove each frame ROI mean; sample variance of each pixel over 16 consecutive frames (n-1 denominator); mean variances across pixels and take square root.",
    "comparison": "Match each group mean before comparing temporal sigma. Mean zero offset is separately assessed with a 0.625 DN correction.",
    "not_measured": "A full shadow-detail ranking or each setting at its own maximum safe exposure."
  },
